      "text": "$CRDO’s ALC demo at OCP next week could be a meaningful milestone for its microLED business.\n\nMicroLEDs emit a broader mix of wavelengths than lasers. That creates a challenge with chromatic dispersion (different wavelengths travel through fiber at different speeds, spreading out the signal and making it harder to read). That’s the concern behind skepticism about reach beyond 10m.\n\nFor Credo, demonstrating stable performance at 30m would help validate its approach and give investors more confidence in the product’s potential.\n\nManagement has described ALCs as a multibillion-dollar opportunity, with an eventual market potentially more than twice the size of AECs (active electrical cables). $LITE $SMTC $AMSSY $APH",
